<p>&nbsp;UpvoteRocket is designed to work directly through a web browser, so there is no software to download or complicated installation process. The service supports more than 400 toplists across the world and is intended for a wide range of private gaming communities, including servers for Perfect World, Pirate King Online, PristonTale, Ragnarok Online, World of Warcraft, Lineage, Guild Wars, RuneScape, Minecraft, Metin2, and other games. The company presents itself as a service trusted by thousands of private server owners and focuses on providing continuous vote delivery without requiring customers to manage the process manually.</p>
<p>&nbsp;The platform is built around a simple objective: helping private servers compete for higher positions on toplists. Campaigns can reportedly be launched in less than two minutes, after which votes can be delivered around the clock. Server owners can select the usernames used for voting, choose the regions associated with those usernames, and configure referral links for individual campaigns. This gives campaign owners control over how their voting activity is presented while allowing them to focus on operating their servers instead of repeatedly submitting votes themselves.</p>
<p>&nbsp;UpvoteRocket also uses a pay-per-success approach. According to the service, credits are only deducted when a vote is successfully completed, meaning unsuccessful attempts do not consume tokens. A live dashboard allows customers to monitor incoming votes and follow campaign activity in real time, providing a central place to observe progress across supported toplists.</p>
<p>&nbsp;The service is positioned as a way for smaller servers to compete with larger communities that already have substantial numbers of players voting every day. Because the highest positions on many toplists are often occupied by established servers with large communities, UpvoteRocket aims to reduce that difference by delivering votes consistently throughout the day and night. The intended result is greater visibility, allowing a server to appear more prominently when potential players browse toplists and search for new communities.</p>
<p>&nbsp;Campaigns can be used to build and maintain a higher position rather than relying only on one-time voting activity. Votes continue to accumulate while the server owner is offline, and recurring campaigns can be scheduled so that they restart automatically. This approach is intended to help maintain a server's position over time while the owner concentrates on development, moderation, community management, and other responsibilities.</p>
<p>&nbsp;The usernames used for campaigns can also be selected by the customer. By using names that are familiar to the server community, vote activity can appear more consistent with the server's established identity. UpvoteRocket therefore presents usernames, campaign settings, and delivery schedules as tools for giving server owners more control over their voting campaigns.</p>
<p>&nbsp;The platform supports a broad selection of games and toplists, with particular coverage for popular private-server categories such as Ragnarok, World of Warcraft, Lineage, Minecraft, RuneScape private servers, and many others. Its website states that more than 400 voting websites are supported, giving private server owners access to a large network of toplist destinations.</p>
<p>&nbsp;For private server owners, toplists can be an important source of exposure because players often discover servers by browsing ranking sites and comparing the communities listed there. UpvoteRocket states that customers can purchase votes for supported toplists at a fixed rate per successful vote, without subscribing to an ongoing plan. The service also provides live campaign tracking and says that additional toplists can be requested when a particular website is not already supported.</p>
<p>&nbsp;Among the toplists supported by the service are XtremeTop100, TopG, Arena-Top100, GameStop200, TopRagnarok, TopRagnarokBR, ArenaTOP100, Silkroad-Servers, MMtop200, eTopGames, RagnaTOP, RankedPrivateServers, RankServeur, Top-Serveurs, MuTop100, RotoP Serv, BestServers, HotServers, Top100Arena, GamingTop100, Top RO Hispano, Gamehot.net, RSPS-List, L2TopZone, Moparscape, Rulocus, RSPS100, Rune-Server, RuneList, RSPS.org, Discadia, Discords.com, Metin2pserver, and GameTop. These websites cover several categories, including MMORPGs, Ragnarok servers, RuneScape private servers, Discord communities, Minecraft and multi-game listings, among others.</p>
<p>&nbsp;The service states that its supported toplist network continues to grow. Customers who cannot find the specific voting website they need can submit a request for that site to be added to the supported list. This allows the service to expand its coverage beyond the toplists already available through its campaign pages.</p>
<p>&nbsp;UpvoteRocket uses a token-based pricing system without a recurring subscription. Customers purchase tokens once and can use them whenever they need, with the service stating that tokens do not expire. The listed packages include Spark at €13.50 for 16 tokens, Blaze at €122 for 160 tokens, Nova at €340 for 530 tokens, and Titan at €875 for 1,900 tokens. The larger packages provide a lower effective cost per token, ranging from approximately €0.844 per token for Spark to €0.461 per token for Titan.</p>
<p>&nbsp;The service also provides answers to common questions from private server owners who are considering purchasing votes. To begin, customers create an UpvoteRocket account, select a supported toplist, provide their public voting URL, choose a token package, configure the desired campaign target, and launch the campaign. The platform states that customers can begin with a smaller campaign and expand it later when additional votes are required.</p>
<p>&nbsp;Other frequently asked questions address the supported toplists and voting websites, how campaigns operate, the cost of purchasing votes, whether failed voting attempts consume tokens, and whether customers can control the pace and timing of vote delivery. The service also discusses campaign tracking, supported games and server types, adding unsupported voting websites, the need for server administrator credentials, the effect of purchased votes on toplist visibility, campaign start times, expected results, and whether a free trial is available.</p>
<p>&nbsp;UpvoteRocket encourages private server owners who cannot find their preferred toplist to submit the website URL for review. The company states that it can explain how support for that website would work and provide a ranking-related assessment before the customer proceeds.</p>
